                <pb facs="0805" n="695" sameAs="frus:frus1931v03/pg695"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/3249: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-12-19T16:00:00+08:00">December 19, 1931—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 19—11:13 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>1105. Following from American Consul General at Mukden: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“December 18, 4 p.m. Reliably informed that Japanese planes bombed
                            Tungliao on the 15th, killing three Chinese. City was in a panic.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>Repeated to Department and Nanking.</p>
                <closer>For the Minister:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >Perkins</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
